feature-003 is intentionally unused.

The MVCC log suffix-naming prompt held 003 while its PR was open, so the
op_variable prompt that merged first took 004. When the MVCC prompt
landed after it, it was renumbered to 005 rather than back to 003, so
that filename order matches the order in which the PRs merged.

Why: re-apply and rebuild carry prompts forward in filename order, and
each stored patch was built on top of the features before it. We judge
that keeping that order is likely (about 65% confidence) more important
than having no gaps in the numbering. Nothing in the scripts needs the
numbers to be consecutive.

This file is deliberately not named *.md: scripts/apply and
scripts/re-apply treat every prompts/*.md as a prompt to apply.

(feature-002 is also absent from nqaf, for a different reason: the fork
already carries an applied feature-002, "Run CI on GitHub-hosted
runners", that nqaf does not track yet.)
